     "title": "Story 0.1 · 📧 Your First Email Address",
     "description": "✨ One account opens Gmail, Google Classroom and Google Forms.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: “The Form Nobody Could Open”\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Bhatt\n\n👵 Mrs. Bhatt is 66 years old and lives in Vadodara. She is a retired nurse.\n\nHer grandson Aarav sends her a message: “Ajji, my school wants you to fill a form. It needs a Gmail address.”\n\nMrs. Bhatt has never made one. “It must be very difficult,” she thinks, and she feels a little worried.\n\n📱 Aarti, a Digital Saathi volunteer, shows her that her phone can:\n• Open the Gmail app\n• Make a new account in a few minutes\n• Use that one account for Gmail, Google Classroom and Google Forms\n\nTogether they type her name, choose a username and a password, and add her phone number.\nMrs. Bhatt writes the password on a small paper and keeps it in her cupboard at home.\n“It was not difficult at all,”* she says, smiling. *“Now I have my very own address.”\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Forget Your Password?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nSome weeks later, Mrs. Bhatt cannot remember her password.\n\nShe taps Forgot password? and Google sends a code to the phone number she added. She types it on the screen, and she is back in.\n\n💡 That is why a phone number matters. And never tell the code to anyone, not even a helper.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Open Gmail and tap Create account\n📱 Open the Gmail app, or go to gmail.com.\n✅ Tap Create account, then choose For myself.\n\n2️⃣ Type your name and choose a username\n✅ Type your first and last name.\n✅ Choose a username. It becomes your address, like name@gmail.com.\n\n3️⃣ Choose a strong password\n✅ Use at least 8 characters, with letters and numbers.\n✅ Type it again to confirm.\n✅ Write it on paper and keep it at home.\n\n4️⃣ Add your phone number and finish\n✅ Add your phone number when asked. It helps you get back in.\n✅ Google may send a code to check it. Type the code on the screen only.\n✅ Read the terms and tap I agree.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: “Help Mrs. Bhatt Make Her Account”\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMrs. Bhatt is creating her Gmail account with Aarti beside her.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Choose a strong password with letters and numbers\n☐ Add her phone number so she can get back in\n☐ Write the password on paper and keep it at home\n☐ Read out the code Google sends to anyone who asks\n☐ Use “123456” as her password\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Choose a strong password with letters and numbers\n✅ Add her phone number so she can get back in\n✅ Write the password on paper and keep it at home\n❌ A code is private. Never share it, not even with a helper\n❌ An easy password is easy for strangers to guess\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Account Creator Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this:\n\n✅ You have your own email address\n✅ One account works for Gmail, Classroom and Google Forms\n✅ You can get back in if you forget your password\n✅ You feel ready for the lessons ahead\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhere will you keep your password safe at home?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
