     "title": "Story 0.2 · 🚪 Lock the Door Behind You",
     "description": "✨ Sign in safely, and always sign out on a shared computer.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: “The Open Inbox”\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Chopra\n\n👴 Mr. Chopra is 70 years old and lives in Ludhiana. He checks his email at a nearby cyber café.\n\nOne morning he reads his email, gets a phone call, and rushes out of the café.\n\nHe forgets to sign out. The next customer sits down at the same computer and sees Mr. Chopra’s inbox.\n\nA kind young man at the café notices and calls him back just in time.\n\n📱 The young man shows him what to remember:\n• Sign in only on gmail.com or the Gmail app\n• Type any code Google sends on the screen only\n• On a shared computer, sign out when you finish\n\nThe next day, Mr. Chopra finishes reading his email. He taps his round picture at the top right and taps Sign out.\n*“Like locking the door behind me,”* he says.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If a Message Asks for Your Password?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Chopra gets a message: “Your account will be closed today. Send your password and OTP to save it.”\n\nHe remembers that Google never asks for a password or OTP by call or message. He ignores it.\n\n💡 When in doubt, do not reply. Open Gmail yourself and look for a real warning there.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Go to the real page\n📱 Open the Gmail app, or type gmail.com yourself.\n✅ Do not sign in from a link in a message.\n\n2️⃣ Sign in\n✅ Type your Gmail address and tap Next.\n✅ Type your password and tap Next.\n\n3️⃣ Keep codes to yourself\n✅ If Google sends a code, type it on the screen only.\n✅ Never read it out on a call.\n\n4️⃣ Sign out on a shared computer\n📱 Tap your round picture at the top right, then tap Sign out.\n✅ Never save your password on a shared or public computer.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: “Help Mr. Chopra Stay Safe”\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMr. Chopra has finished reading his email at a cyber café.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do before he leaves? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Tap his picture and choose Sign out\n☐ Close the browser window after signing out\n☐ Never save his password on that computer\n☐ Just close the tab and walk away\n☐ Tell a caller who says “I am from Google” his OTP\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Tap his picture and choose Sign out\n✅ Close the browser window after signing out\n✅ Never save his password on that computer\n❌ The next person may still see his inbox\n❌ Google never asks for an OTP by phone\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Safe Sign-Out Pro Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this:\n\n✅ Your emails stay private on shared computers\n✅ You sign in only on pages you can trust\n✅ You are not fooled by messages that ask for a password or code\n✅ You feel in control of your account\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich computers do you use that are not your own? Will you remember to sign out?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
