    {
     "title": "Story 1.2 · 👓 Read With Confidence",
     "description": "✨ Bigger letters, and a phone that reads aloud to you. No more squinting.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Message I Could Finally Read\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Iyer\n\n👴 Mr. Iyer is 71 years old and lives in Chennai. He used to be a bank clerk and he still loves reading.\n\nLately, his eyes get tired quickly. The letters on his phone look like tiny ants.\n\nOne evening, a message arrives from the gas agency about his cylinder delivery.\nHe holds the phone close, then far, then close again. He cannot read the time slot.\nHe misses the delivery, and he is too shy to ask anyone for help.\n\nThe next Sunday, his daughter Meena visits.\nShe makes the letters bigger and turns on Select to Speak.\n\n📱 His phone can now:\n• Show big, clear letters\n• Read any text aloud when he taps it\n• Help him even when he has no glasses\n\nThe next message arrives. Mr. Iyer reads it by himself, and the phone reads the time slot aloud.\n*\"My phone is finally speaking my language,\"* he laughs.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Forgot Your Glasses?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Menon is at the vegetable market. Her glasses are at home.\nA message arrives from the pharmacy about her husband's medicine.\n\nShe taps the message, and her phone reads it aloud.\nShe learns that the medicine is ready for pickup today.\n\n💡 In a crowded place, use earphones for private messages.\n💡 Never ask a stranger to read your bank message or your OTP.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone. Use the search box in Settings if you cannot find a name.)\n\n1️⃣ Make the Letters Bigger\n📱 Open: Settings → Display → Font size\n\n✅ Slide towards bigger letters until reading feels easy.\n\n2️⃣ Turn On Select to Speak\n📱 Open: Settings → Accessibility → Select to Speak\n\n✅ Turn it ON.\n\n3️⃣ Listen\n✅ Tap any text on the screen.\n✅ Your phone reads it aloud.\n\n4️⃣ Keep It Private\n✅ Use earphones for bank and health messages.\n✅ Never share your OTP with anyone who offers to \"read it for you\".\n\n📱 iPhone: Use Spoken Content (Settings → Accessibility).\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Sunita's Tiny Message\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nSunita received an important bank message. The words are too small to read, and she does not want anyone to read it for her.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat can Sunita do on her own phone? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Make the text bigger in Settings → Display → Font size\n☐ Turn on Select to Speak, then tap the message\n☐ Use earphones so only she hears it\n☐ Ask a stranger at the bus stop to read it aloud\n☐ Ignore the message\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Make the text bigger in Settings → Display → Font size\n✅ Turn on Select to Speak, then tap the message\n✅ Use earphones so only she hears it\n❌ A stranger should never read your bank messages\n❌ Ignoring an important message can cause trouble\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Smart Reader Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on these settings:\n\n✅ You can read your own messages, bills and news\n✅ Your eyes get less tired\n✅ Your phone can read to you when you have no glasses\n✅ You keep your messages private and feel independent\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich message or paper do you usually ask someone else to read for you? How would it feel to read it yourself?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
