    {
     "title": "Story 1.3 · 📄 The Pocket Photocopier",
     "description": "✨ Turn any paper into a clear PDF and send it on WhatsApp in a minute.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Closed on Sunday, Solved in a Minute\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Kulkarni\n\n👩 Mrs. Kulkarni is 64 years old and lives in Kolhapur. She was a school teacher and she keeps her papers neat.\n\nOn Sunday, her son Aniket calls from Pune in a hurry.\n\"Aai, the insurance office needs a copy of Baba's policy paper today.\"\n\nThe paper is in her cupboard.\nBut the photocopy shop is far away, and it is closed on Sunday.\n\nShe tries a photo with her phone. It comes out dark and crooked, with her shadow on it.\nAniket cannot read it.\n\nThen her neighbour's daughter, Isha, shows her the scanner hidden in her phone.\n\n📱 Her phone can:\n• Find the edges of the paper by itself\n• Make the picture clean and straight\n• Save it as a clear PDF\n• Send it on WhatsApp\n\nIn under a minute, the PDF reaches Aniket.\n\"Aai, you are better than a photocopy shop!\"\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the Paper Could Get Lost or Spoilt?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Rehman keeps his doctor's reports and prescriptions in a cupboard.\nLast monsoon, rain water spoilt some of his old papers.\n\nNow he scans them and keeps clear copies on his phone.\nWhen the hospital counter asks for a copy, he sends the PDF in a minute.\n\n💡 Private papers, like your Aadhaar or bank papers, should go only to people you know and trust. Never post them in a big group.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. The Google Drive app is free and is usually already on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Open Google Drive\n✅ Open the Google Drive app.\n\n2️⃣ Start the Scanner\n📱 Tap +, then tap Scan.\n\n3️⃣ Scan the Paper\n✅ Place the paper flat, in good light.\n✅ Point the camera at it and tap the round button.\n✅ Move the corners if the edges are not exact.\n\n4️⃣ Save and Send\n✅ Tap Save. It becomes a clear PDF.\n✅ Share it on WhatsApp.\n\n📱 iPhone: Use Notes → Scan Documents.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Prakash's Electricity Bill\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nPrakash Bhai's housing society secretary asks him for a copy of his electricity bill on WhatsApp. The photocopy shop is far away.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should Prakash Bhai do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Open Google Drive, tap + and then Scan\n☐ Place the paper flat in good light\n☐ Save it as a PDF and send it on WhatsApp\n☐ Take a blurry photo from far away in a dark corner\n☐ Post the bill in a big public group\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Open Google Drive, tap + and then Scan\n✅ Place the paper flat in good light\n✅ Save it as a PDF and send it on WhatsApp\n❌ A blurry, dark photo cannot be read\n❌ A bill should never be posted in a public group\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Paper-to-PDF Pro Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You save a trip to the photocopy shop\n✅ You save time and money\n✅ You send clear papers instead of crooked photos\n✅ You keep important papers safe, even if the paper is lost\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich paper in your cupboard would you hate to lose? Who could you send a clear copy to?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 1.4 · 🔒 The Safe Handover",
     "description": "✨ Let the little ones watch their rhymes, without wandering into your messages.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Aarav Watches, Aaji's Phone Stays Safe\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Deshmukh\n\n👵 Mrs. Deshmukh is 62 years old and lives in Mumbai with her son's family.\n\nHer grandson Aarav is five. Every evening he runs to her: *\"Aaji, phone! Rhymes!\"*\n\nLast week, while watching his rhyme, he tapped a corner of the screen.\nHe landed in her WhatsApp and sent a string of smileys and a blank voice note to her friend.\n\nNow she feels nervous every time she hands over the phone.\nShe sits right beside him and keeps taking it back.\n\nThen her daughter-in-law, Pooja, shows her App pinning.\n\n📱 Her phone can now:\n• Stay on one app only\n• Ask for her PIN before anyone can leave that app\n• Keep her chats, photos and payment apps out of reach\n\nAarav taps everywhere, but the screen stays on his rhymes.\nMrs. Deshmukh sips her tea in peace.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Cannot Watch the Child Every Second?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Sheikh is cooking for a family wedding.\nHer cousin's eight-year-old, Zoya, wants to play a game on her phone.\n\nThe phone has a payment app, photos and chats.\nBefore she hands it over, Mrs. Sheikh pins the game.\n\nZoya can play. She cannot open the payment app or the chats, even by accident,\nbecause leaving the game needs Mrs. Sheikh's PIN.\n\n💡 Never tell the child your PIN.\n💡 When you take the phone back, enter your PIN and unpin the app.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone. Use the search box in Settings and type \"pin\" if you cannot find it.)\n\n1️⃣ Turn On App Pinning\n📱 Open: Settings → Security (or search \"pin\")\n\n✅ Turn App pinning ON.\n✅ If it asks, choose to ask for your PIN before unpinning.\n\n2️⃣ Open the App\n✅ Open the app you want the child to use, for example the rhyme video.\n\n3️⃣ Pin It\n📱 Open Recent apps (use the button or swipe your phone uses for this).\n\n✅ Tap the app's icon at the top.\n✅ Choose Pin.\n\n4️⃣ Hand Over the Phone\n✅ The child cannot leave that app without your PIN.\n✅ When you take the phone back, enter your PIN to unpin.\n\n📱 iPhone: Use Guided Access.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Neelam's Granddaughter\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nNeelam's granddaughter Riya, 6, wants to watch a drawing video. Neelam's phone has WhatsApp, photos and a payment app.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should Neelam do before handing over the phone? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Turn on App pinning in Settings → Security\n☐ Open the video app, go to Recent apps, tap its icon and choose Pin\n☐ Make sure her PIN is needed to leave the app\n☐ Tell Riya the phone's PIN so she can \"help\"\n☐ Hand over the phone with all the apps open\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Turn on App pinning in Settings → Security\n✅ Open the video app, go to Recent apps, tap its icon and choose Pin\n✅ Make sure her PIN is needed to leave the app\n❌ A child should never know your PIN\n❌ An open phone lets her tap into other apps\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Child-Safe Guardian Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this setting:\n\n✅ Your messages, photos and apps stay private\n✅ Your money stays safe from accidental taps\n✅ No more wrong calls or messages\n✅ You can relax and enjoy time with your grandchild\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhen a child uses your phone, what worries you most? How could pinning one app help?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 1.5 · 🗣️ Your Pocket Assistant",
     "description": "✨ Just say it, and your phone will remember your medicines and bills.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"I Told My Phone, and It Remembered\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Nair\n\n👴 Mr. Nair is 74 years old and lives in Kochi. He retired from the railways.\n\nEvery morning he has a small routine: tea, newspaper, and a tablet for his blood pressure at 9 am.\n\nThis month, his granddaughter's wedding fills the house with guests.\nHis routine has become muddled.\n\nTwice this week he forgot his 9 am tablet.\nThen a letter came: his electricity bill was late, and he had to pay a late fee.\n\n*\"My memory is not what it used to be,\"* he says sadly.\n\nThat evening, his son Anil says: *\"Appa, you do not need to remember everything. Just tell your phone.\"*\n\n📱 His phone can:\n• Set a reminder when you speak, with no typing\n• Remind you at the right time\n• Remember medicines, bills and more\n\nMr. Nair says: \"Hey Google, remind me to take my medicine every day at 9 am.\"\nThe phone confirms.\n\nNext morning at 9, the phone rings gently. He takes his tablet and taps Done.\nOn the 5th, it reminds him to pay the bill, with no late fee.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If Typing Is Hard, or Your Hands Are Busy?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Krishnan has stiff fingers from arthritis.\nToday her hands are covered in flour while she makes chapatis.\nShe remembers she must book a blood test.\n\nShe does not wash her hands or look for her phone's keyboard.\nShe simply says: \"Hey Google, remind me to book my blood test tomorrow at 10 am.\"\n\nDone in seconds, with no typing.\n\n💡 Reminders help you remember. They do not replace your doctor's advice. Take medicines exactly as your doctor told you.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. \"Hey Google\" must be turned on. If your phone does not answer, ask a family member to switch it on once.)\n\n1️⃣ Wake Up Your Phone\n✅ Say clearly: \"Hey Google\"\n✅ Wait for the phone to listen.\n\n2️⃣ Set a Medicine Reminder\n✅ Say: \"Remind me to take my medicine every day at 9 am.\"\n\n3️⃣ Set a Bill Reminder\n✅ Say: \"Remind me to pay the electricity bill on the 5th.\"\n\n4️⃣ When It Rings\n✅ Your phone reminds you on time.\n✅ Tap Done when you have finished.\n\n💡 Speak slowly in a quiet place. If the phone did not understand, say it again.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Kusum's Two Reminders\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nKusum wants a reminder for her sugar tablet every evening at 8 pm, and a reminder to pay her gas bill on the 10th.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should Kusum say to her phone? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ \"Hey Google, remind me to take my sugar tablet every day at 8 pm.\"\n☐ \"Hey Google, remind me to pay the gas bill on the 10th.\"\n☐ \"Hey Google, forget my bills.\"\n☐ Say nothing and hope she remembers\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ \"Hey Google, remind me to take my sugar tablet every day at 8 pm.\"\n✅ \"Hey Google, remind me to pay the gas bill on the 10th.\"\n❌ Telling the phone to forget will not help\n❌ Hoping to remember is exactly the problem\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Reminder Master Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You do not miss your medicine time\n✅ You pay bills on time, with no late fees\n✅ You need no typing, even with stiff fingers\n✅ You feel calm and independent\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhat are the three things you most worry about forgetting? Which one will you tell your phone first?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 1.6 · 🔋 Full Day, Full Power",
     "description": "✨ Simple habits that keep your phone alive from morning till night.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Phone That Lasted Till the Video Call\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Joshi\n\n👵 Mrs. Joshi is 67 years old and lives in Nagpur.\n\nHer granddaughter Ananya studies in another country.\nThey have a promise: a video call every evening at 8 o'clock.\n\nBut lately, Mrs. Joshi's phone goes dead around 5 or 6 in the evening.\nYesterday the call ended halfway because the battery ran out.\nAnanya was sad, and Mrs. Joshi felt helpless.\n\n\"This phone gets tired before I do!\"\n\nHer neighbour, Mr. Kelkar, shows her four small habits.\n\n📱 Her phone can last longer if she:\n• Turns on Battery Saver\n• Keeps the screen brightness low\n• Closes the apps she is not using\n• Switches off Location and Bluetooth when she does not need them\n\nAt 8 o'clock that evening, her phone still has enough charge for the whole video call.\n\"My phone lasted the whole day, just like me!\"\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Cannot Charge Your Phone for a Long Time?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Singh is travelling by train for many hours.\nThere is no charging point near his seat, and his phone is getting low.\nHe still needs it to show his ticket and to call his daughter at the station.\n\nHe turns on Battery Saver, keeps the brightness low, closes unused apps,\nand switches off Location and Bluetooth. He does not watch videos on the way.\n\nHis phone lasts until the station, and he calls his daughter in time.\n\n💡 If your battery is very low, keep the last bit of charge for the most important thing: a call to your family.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone. Use the search box in Settings if you cannot find a name.)\n\n1️⃣ Turn On Battery Saver\n📱 Open: Settings → Battery\n\n✅ Turn Battery Saver ON.\n\n2️⃣ Keep the Screen Dim\n✅ Swipe down from the top of the screen.\n✅ Move the brightness slider towards low.\n\n3️⃣ Close Unused Apps\n✅ Open Recent apps.\n✅ Close the apps you are not using.\n\n4️⃣ Switch Off What You Do Not Need\n✅ Switch off Location and Bluetooth when you do not need them.\n✅ Switch them on again when you do, for example Location when you use Maps.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Jaya's Dying Phone\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nJaya's phone is dead by 3 o'clock every afternoon. She wants it to last till bedtime.\n\n❓ Question\nWhich habits will help? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Turn on Battery Saver in Settings → Battery\n☐ Keep the screen brightness low\n☐ Close the apps she is not using\n☐ Switch off Location and Bluetooth when she does not need them\n☐ Keep the screen at full brightness all day\n☐ Keep ten apps open all day, \"just in case\"\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Turn on Battery Saver in Settings → Battery\n✅ Keep the screen brightness low\n✅ Close the apps she is not using\n✅ Switch off Location and Bluetooth when she does not need them\n❌ A very bright screen uses more battery\n❌ Many open apps use more battery\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Battery Boss Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on these habits:\n\n✅ Your phone lasts through the day\n✅ You do not have to hunt for a charger\n✅ Your phone is ready for calls, tickets and emergencies\n✅ You feel less worried\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAt what time does your phone usually go dead? What is the most important thing you need it for then?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    }
