     "title": "Story 2.1 · 🔍 Your Magic Lens",
     "description": "✨ Point your camera at anything, and your phone can translate it, name it or copy it.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Board I Couldn't Read\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Reddy\n\n👴 Mr. Reddy is 69 years old and lives in Hyderabad. He is visiting his daughter in Pune for a month.\n\nHe loves his morning walk, but in Pune every shop board and bus board is written in Marathi.\nHe does not read Marathi.\n\nOne morning he wants to find the dairy his daughter mentioned.\nHe stands in the lane, looking at boards he cannot read. He feels lost, and he does not like to keep asking people.\n\nThen his granddaughter Sneha shows him the camera icon in the Google search bar. It is called Google Lens.\n\n📱 His phone can:\n• Translate the words on a board into his language\n• Search to tell him what something is\n• Copy the words so he can use them\n\nHe points the camera at the board and chooses Translate.\nThe words change into his own language: *“Sai Dairy and Sweets.”*\n\n*“So the phone has eyes now,”* he laughs, and walks into the shop.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Cannot Read a Medicine Strip, or Do Not Know a Plant?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Bhatt, 64, is given a medicine strip with a name she cannot read.\nShe points the camera at it and chooses Text, to copy the words, or Search, to find out what it is.\n\nIn the garden, her neighbour's plant has pretty flowers, but nobody knows its name.\nShe points the camera and chooses Search.\n\n💡 Lens helps you read and learn. For medicines, always follow your doctor's advice.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Open the Google Search Bar\n✅ Find the Google search bar on your home screen, or open the Google app.\n\n2️⃣ Tap the Camera Icon\n📱 Tap the camera icon. This is Google Lens.\n\n3️⃣ Point at Something\n✅ Point the camera at a sign, a medicine strip or a plant.\n\n4️⃣ Choose What You Want\n✅ Translate: change the words into your language\n✅ Search: find out what it is\n✅ Text: copy the words\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Reddy in the Lane\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nA shop board is written in a language Mr. Reddy cannot read.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat can he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Tap the camera icon (Google Lens) in the Google search bar\n☐ Point the camera at the board\n☐ Choose Translate\n☐ Take a photo and delete it\n☐ Ask the phone to switch off\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Tap the camera icon (Google Lens) in the Google search bar\n✅ Point the camera at the board\n✅ Choose Translate\n❌ Deleting a photo will not translate anything\n❌ Switching off the phone will not help\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Lens Explorer Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You can read boards and signs in other languages\n✅ You can find out what a plant or object is\n✅ You can copy words without typing them\n✅ You feel less lost in new places\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhere did you last feel lost because you could not read a sign or a label? How would Lens have helped?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
