     "title": "Story 2.3 · 🧒 Safe Screens for Little Eyes",
     "description": "✨ Let children watch videos made for them, and keep grown-up videos away.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Video That Should Not Have Appeared\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Nambiar\n\n👵 Mrs. Nambiar is 61 years old and lives in Kochi. Her grandson Kabir is six.\n\nKabir loves cartoons on her phone.\nOne afternoon, while she is in the kitchen, the next video on regular YouTube is not for children.\nIt is loud and frightening, and Kabir comes running to her, wide-eyed.\n\nMrs. Nambiar is upset with herself. She does not want this to happen again.\n\nHer son shows her the YouTube Kids app.\n\n📱 Her phone can:\n• Show videos made for children in the YouTube Kids app\n• Keep the grown-up videos away from small eyes\n• Let Kabir watch his cartoons without worry\n\nThe next day she installs YouTube Kids, and Kabir watches his cartoons.\nNothing frightening appears.\n*“Now I can finish cooking in peace,”* she smiles.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If an Older Child Uses Regular YouTube?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Nambiar's granddaughter Mira is 11 and likes regular YouTube for her school projects.\n\nOn regular YouTube, her mother turns on Restricted Mode.\nIt helps hide videos meant for adults.\n\n💡 No setting is perfect. Sit with children sometimes, and ask them to tell you if anything upsets them.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ For Young Children\n✅ Install the YouTube Kids app from the Play Store.\n✅ Open it for your child.\n\n2️⃣ For Older Children on Regular YouTube\n📱 Open the YouTube app.\n✅ Tap your profile picture.\n\n3️⃣ Open Settings\n📱 Open: Settings → General\n\n4️⃣ Turn On Restricted Mode\n✅ Turn Restricted Mode ON.\n✅ This helps hide videos meant for adults.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Kabir's Cartoons\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMrs. Nambiar wants Kabir, 6, to watch only cartoons made for children.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Use the YouTube Kids app for Kabir\n☐ On regular YouTube, turn on Restricted Mode for older children\n☐ Sit with the children sometimes and ask if anything upset them\n☐ Let a six-year-old browse regular YouTube alone\n☐ Switch off the phone's sound\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Use the YouTube Kids app for Kabir\n✅ On regular YouTube, turn on Restricted Mode for older children\n✅ Sit with the children sometimes and ask if anything upset them\n❌ A young child should not browse regular YouTube alone\n❌ Switching off the sound does not hide what appears on the screen\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Safe Screen Guardian Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this setting:\n\n✅ Children watch videos made for their age\n✅ Grown-up videos stay out of sight\n✅ You worry less when a child holds your phone\n✅ Children enjoy safe fun\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich videos do your grandchildren watch? When did you last sit with them to see what they were watching?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
