     "title": "Story 2.4 · 🔐 Your Spare Key",
     "description": "✨ A recovery number and email mean you will never be locked out of your Google account.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Password I Forgot\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Banerjee\n\n👴 Mr. Banerjee is 70 years old and lives in Kolkata. He is a retired schoolteacher.\n\nHis Gmail holds everything: his pension papers, his old photos, his daughter's emails from abroad.\n\nOne morning, after his phone is updated, it asks for his password.\nHe types what he thinks it is. Wrong.\nHe types another. Wrong again.\n\nHis heart sinks. *“What if I can never open my emails again?”*\n\nHis daughter calls him. *“Baba, do you remember adding a recovery phone number and email?”*\nHe had added them last year, when she visited and helped him.\n\nThe phone sends a code to his recovery number, and he sets a new password.\nHis emails are back, safe.\n\n*“Like a spare key in the neighbour's house,”* he says.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Lose Your Phone?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Joshi, 66, loses her phone on a train.\nShe needs to sign in to her Google account on a new phone.\n\nBecause she added a recovery phone number and a recovery email, Google can confirm that it is really her and let her back in.\n\n💡 Also write your password down and keep it somewhere safe at home. Do not keep the paper in your wallet.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Open Your Google Account\n📱 Open: Settings → Google → Manage your Google Account\n\n2️⃣ Go to Security\n✅ Tap Security.\n\n3️⃣ Add Recovery Details\n✅ Add a recovery phone number.\n✅ Add a recovery email.\n✅ Use a number and an email that you can really reach, for example a family member's.\n\n4️⃣ Write Your Password Down\n✅ Write your password on paper.\n✅ Keep the paper somewhere safe at home.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Banerjee's Spare Key\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMr. Banerjee wants to make sure he is never locked out of his Google account.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Add a recovery phone number\n☐ Add a recovery email\n☐ Write his password down and keep it safe at home\n☐ Tell his password to a stranger who calls\n☐ Use \"1234\" for every account\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Add a recovery phone number\n✅ Add a recovery email\n✅ Write his password down and keep it safe at home\n❌ Never tell your password to anyone who calls you\n❌ Simple passwords like “1234” are easy to guess\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Account Keeper Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this setting:\n\n✅ You can get back into your account if you forget the password\n✅ Your emails, photos and papers stay safe\n✅ A new phone is easy to set up\n✅ You feel calm instead of panicked\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWho is the one person whose phone number you would trust as your recovery number? Have you asked them?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
