    {
     "title": "Story 3.3 · 🔕 Peace and Quiet",
     "description": "✨ Mute noisy groups, and stop strangers from adding you to new ones.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Three Hundred Messages by Morning\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. D'Souza\n\n👵 Mrs. D'Souza is 66 years old and lives in Mangaluru. She loves her church friends' group and her family group.\n\nBut one morning she wakes up to 300 new messages.\nGood-morning pictures, jokes, forwarded videos, one after another, from groups she hardly reads.\nHer phone buzzes all night, and her sleep is disturbed.\n\nAnd that is not all. Last week, a stranger added her to a group about “easy money.”\nShe does not even know the people there.\n\nHer son shows her two settings.\n\n📱 Her phone can:\n• Mute a noisy group, so it stops buzzing\n• Let only her contacts add her to groups\n• Keep strangers out of her chats\n\nShe taps a group's name, chooses Mute notifications → Always.\nThen she opens WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Groups and chooses “My contacts.”\n\nThat night, she sleeps well. *“Now my phone is quiet and my chats are mine,”* she says.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If a Stranger Adds You to a Strange Group?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Prabhu, 70, finds himself in a group for “fast profit” that he never joined.\nHe is worried it is a scam.\n\nBecause he chose “My contacts,” from then on only people saved in his phone can add him.\n\n💡 If a group looks strange or asks for money, do not reply and do not click on links. You can leave the group.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(WhatsApp on Android and iPhone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Mute a Noisy Group\n📱 Open the group and tap the group's name at the top.\n\n2️⃣ Choose Mute Notifications\n✅ Tap Mute notifications → Always.\n\n3️⃣ Open Privacy Settings\n📱 Open: WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Groups\n\n4️⃣ Choose Who Can Add You\n✅ Choose “My contacts.”\n✅ Now strangers cannot add you to groups.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mrs. D'Souza's Quiet Night\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMrs. D'Souza's phone buzzes all night, and strangers keep adding her to groups.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Tap a noisy group's name and choose Mute notifications → Always\n☐ Open WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Groups\n☐ Choose “My contacts”\n☐ Reply to every stranger who adds her\n☐ Delete WhatsApp for ever\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Tap a noisy group's name and choose Mute notifications → Always\n✅ Open WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Groups\n✅ Choose “My contacts”\n❌ Replying to strangers invites more trouble\n❌ Deleting WhatsApp also loses the family group\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Calm Chat Keeper Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on these settings:\n\n✅ Your phone stops buzzing all night\n✅ Strangers cannot add you to strange groups\n✅ You still get messages from family and friends\n✅ You feel in control of your chats\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich group on your phone is the noisiest? Would you like to mute it tonight?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 3.4 · 📵 The Unknown Caller Shield",
     "description": "✨ Stop calls from strangers ringing on WhatsApp, and still see who called.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Afternoon Nap\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Chauhan\n\n👴 Mr. Chauhan is 69 years old and lives in Jaipur. After lunch, he likes a short afternoon nap.\n\nBut lately, strange numbers keep calling him on WhatsApp.\nSometimes the phone rings three times in an hour.\nHe does not know who is calling, and he is a little scared.\n\nOnce he picked up, and a stranger started talking about a “prize.” He cut the call, but he felt uneasy for hours.\n\nHis nephew Ishaan shows him a setting called Silence unknown callers.\n\n📱 His phone can:\n• Silence WhatsApp calls from numbers not in his contacts\n• Still show those calls in his call list\n• Ring normally for family and friends\n\nHe opens WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Calls and turns on Silence unknown callers.\n\nThe next afternoon, he naps in peace.\nWhen he wakes, he sees two missed calls from unknown numbers in his call list. He ignores them.\n\n*“My phone has a guard at the door,”* he says.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If a Real Person, Like a Delivery Boy, Calls?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Anand, 65, is waiting for a delivery.\nThe delivery boy's number is not in her contacts, so her phone does not ring.\n\nLater, she sees the call in her call list, because silenced calls still show there.\nShe calls him back, and the parcel arrives.\n\n💡 Check your call list once in a while, so you do not miss anything important.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(WhatsApp on Android and iPhone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Open WhatsApp Settings\n✅ Open WhatsApp and go to Settings.\n\n2️⃣ Open Privacy\n📱 Tap Privacy.\n\n3️⃣ Open Calls\n📱 Tap Calls.\n\n4️⃣ Silence Unknown Callers\n✅ Turn on Silence unknown callers.\n✅ Calls from numbers not in your contacts will not ring. They still show in your call list.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Chauhan's Quiet Afternoon\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nStrange numbers keep calling Mr. Chauhan on WhatsApp in the afternoon.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Open WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Calls\n☐ Turn on Silence unknown callers\n☐ Check his call list now and then\n☐ Answer every unknown call and share his details\n☐ Delete all his contacts\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Open WhatsApp Settings → Privacy → Calls\n✅ Turn on Silence unknown callers\n✅ Check his call list now and then\n❌ Never share your details with unknown callers\n❌ If contacts are deleted, even family calls will be silenced\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Call Shield Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes on this setting:\n\n✅ Strangers cannot disturb your rest\n✅ Family and friends still reach you\n✅ You can still see who called and call back if needed\n✅ You feel safer from scam calls\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAt what time of day do unknown calls disturb you most? Would you like your phone to stay silent then?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 3.5 · 🖥️ Show Me Your Screen",
     "description": "✨ Share your screen on a video call, so family can guide you step by step.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Setting I Could Not Find\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Thakur\n\n👵 Mrs. Thakur is 67 years old and lives in Nashik. Her son Aditya lives in Bengaluru.\n\nHer phone shows a message about an update, and she does not know what to press.\nAditya tries to explain on the phone: *“Amma, go to Settings, then tap the third one…”*\nMrs. Thakur gets confused. *“Which Settings? Where?”*\nBoth get tired and a little cross.\n\nThen Aditya says: *“Amma, let me see your screen.”*\n\n📱 Her phone can:\n• Share her screen during a WhatsApp video call\n• Let Aditya see exactly what she sees\n• Let him guide her step by step\n\nShe taps the share-screen button during the video call.\nAditya sees her phone and says: *“Amma, tap the gear icon on the left. Yes, that one.”*\n\nIn five minutes, it is done. *“Why did we not do this before?”* she laughs.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If Your Bank or Payment App Is Open?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Pillai, 70, is helped by his grandson on a video call.\nBefore sharing his screen, he closes his bank and payment apps.\n\nThat way, his grandson sees only what he needs to, and no private money details.\n\n💡 Share your screen only with people you know and trust. Never share it with someone who called you out of the blue.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(WhatsApp on Android and iPhone. Menu names can differ a little on your phone.)\n\n1️⃣ Start a Video Call\n✅ Start a WhatsApp video call with a family member you trust.\n\n2️⃣ Close Private Apps\n✅ Close your bank and payment apps before you share.\n\n3️⃣ Share Your Screen\n📱 During the video call, tap the share-screen button.\n\n4️⃣ Follow the Guidance\n✅ Your family member sees your screen and guides you.\n✅ Stop sharing when you are done.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mrs. Thakur's Update\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMrs. Thakur's son wants to guide her through a phone setting on a video call.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Start a WhatsApp video call with her son\n☐ Close her bank and payment apps first\n☐ Tap the share-screen button\n☐ Stop sharing when the job is done\n☐ Share her screen with a stranger who called her\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Start a WhatsApp video call with her son\n✅ Close her bank and payment apps first\n✅ Tap the share-screen button\n✅ Stop sharing when the job is done\n❌ Never share your screen with a stranger who called you\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Screen Helper Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ Family can guide you step by step\n✅ No more confusing instructions on the phone\n✅ You solve problems faster and feel less stressed\n✅ You learn new things with your family\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich phone problem would you like your family to guide you through, by looking at your screen?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    },
    {
     "title": "Story 3.6 · 🔗 One Tap to Join",
     "description": "✨ Join a class or family meeting with just one link.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Didi's Birthday on Zoom\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Naik\n\n👴 Mr. Naik is 71 years old and lives in Panaji. His younger sister, Didi, lives in Canada, and her birthday is on Sunday.\n\nThe family has planned a video meeting with everyone, in different cities and countries.\nHis niece sends a link on WhatsApp: *“Uncle, tap this at 6 pm.”*\n\nMr. Naik is nervous. *“What if I press the wrong thing? What if I cannot find the meeting?”*\nHe has never joined a meeting before.\n\nHis grandson Neil sits with him and shows him how simple it is.\n\n📱 His phone can:\n• Open the meeting with one tap on the link\n• Show his own name so others know it is him\n• Let him join and see his whole family\n\nAt 6 pm, he taps the link, allows the camera and microphone, checks his name and taps Join.\n\nThe screen fills with faces: Didi, cousins, nieces, all singing.\n*“I am at the party, from my own sofa,”* he says, delighted.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If It Is a Class and Not a Party?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Kamat, 66, joins a free online learning class with a link from the teacher.\nAt class time, she taps the Google Meet link.\n\nShe allows the camera and microphone and taps Join.\n\n💡 Join only links sent by people you know. Do not tap meeting links from strangers.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Set It Up\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n(Android phone. Google Meet and Zoom work in a similar way. Menu names can differ a little.)\n\n1️⃣ Receive the Link\n✅ Someone sends a Google Meet or Zoom link.\n\n2️⃣ Tap the Link at the Meeting Time\n✅ Tap the link when the meeting is about to start.\n\n3️⃣ Allow Camera and Microphone\n✅ Tap Allow for the camera and the microphone, so others can see and hear you.\n\n4️⃣ Check Your Name and Join\n✅ Check that your name is right.\n✅ Tap Join.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Naik's Birthday Meeting\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMr. Naik receives a meeting link from his niece for a family birthday on video.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Tap the link at the meeting time\n☐ Allow the camera and microphone\n☐ Check his name\n☐ Tap Join\n☐ Tap a meeting link sent by an unknown stranger\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Tap the link at the meeting time\n✅ Allow the camera and microphone\n✅ Check his name\n✅ Tap Join\n❌ Join only links sent by people you know\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Meeting Ready Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You can join family functions from far away\n✅ You can attend classes and meetings from home\n✅ You do not have to travel for every event\n✅ You feel connected to people you love\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich family member or friend far away would you most like to see on a video meeting?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
    }
