     "title": "Story 4.1 · 🚨 The Call That Wasn't Police",
     "description": "✨ Real police never arrest anyone on a video call. Hang up and call 1930.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Officer on the Screen\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Ghosh\n\n👴 Mr. Ghosh is 70 years old and lives in Kolkata. He is a retired bank manager, and he has never had a problem with the law.\n\nOne afternoon, an unknown number calls him on video.\nA man in a police uniform sits in front of a desk. *“Mr. Ghosh, a parcel in your name has illegal items. You are under digital arrest. Do not hang up. Do not tell anyone. Transfer money to settle the case.”*\n\nMr. Ghosh's hands go cold. His heart pounds. He is frightened.\n\nBut a line from the Digital Saathi class comes back to him: “Police never arrest anyone on a video call, and never ask for money to ‘settle a case.’”\n\n📱 What he remembers:\n• Real police, the CBI or courts never arrest anyone on a video call\n• They never ask for money to settle a case\n• A frightening call in uniform is a scam\n\nHe takes a breath and hangs up.\nThen he calls 1930, the cyber crime helpline, and tells them.\n\nHis family hears about it that evening, and they all feel relieved. *“You did the right thing, Baba.”*\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the Caller Says “Do Not Tell Anyone”?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Iyer, 65, gets a similar call. The caller says: *“Do not tell your family or you will be in trouble.”*\n\nThat is a big warning sign. Scammers want you alone and scared, so you do not think clearly.\n\nShe hangs up and tells her son at once.\n\n💡 If anyone in uniform threatens you on a call, hang up and call 1930 or your local police.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ What To Do — Step by Step\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Stay Calm\n✅ Take a deep breath. A real arrest does not happen over a video call.\n\n2️⃣ Do Not Pay Anything\n✅ Never send money to “settle a case.”\n✅ Never share your Aadhaar, bank details or OTP.\n\n3️⃣ Hang Up\n✅ Cut the call. You do not have to be polite.\n\n4️⃣ Call for Help\n📱 Call 1930 or your local police.\n✅ Tell a family member at once.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Ghosh's Afternoon\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nA person in police uniform calls Mr. Ghosh on video and says he is under “digital arrest” and must pay money.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Stay calm and not pay anything\n☐ Hang up\n☐ Call 1930 or the local police\n☐ Tell a family member\n☐ Transfer money to “settle the case”\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Stay calm and not pay anything\n✅ Hang up\n✅ Call 1930 or the local police\n✅ Tell a family member\n❌ Never send money to settle a case, because real police do not ask for it\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Scam Stopper Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You know that real police never arrest anyone on a video call\n✅ You do not lose money to frightening calls\n✅ You know who to call: 1930 or your local police\n✅ You feel calm and strong, not scared\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nIf a frightening call came today, who is the first person you would tell?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
