     "title": "Story 4.2 · 🚩 Spot the Fake Message",
     "description": "✨ KYC, electricity and parcel messages with a link or a number are fake. Check only in the official app.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Your Electricity Will Be Cut Tonight\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mrs. Pandey\n\n👵 Mrs. Pandey is 62 years old and lives in Lucknow. She lives with her husband and pays all the household bills on time.\n\nOne evening, her phone buzzes with a message:\n“Your electricity will be cut tonight! Call this number now.”\n\nHer husband is resting, and the fan is running. Her heart skips.\nShe is about to call the number.\n\nThen she remembers a lesson: messages that rush you, with a link or a number, are fake.\n\n📱 She remembers:\n• “Your KYC is expiring”, “your electricity will be cut tonight” or “your parcel is stuck” are common fake messages\n• A link or a number in them is the trap\n• The only safe place to check is the official app or the office\n\nShe does not call. She opens the official electricity app.\nIt shows: *No dues. Next bill on the 15th.*\n\n*“It was a trick!”* she says. She deletes the message.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the Message Has Your Name and Looks Real?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMr. Verma, 68, gets a message: *“Your parcel is stuck. Update your address here.”* It even has his name.\n\nScammers can find names easily. A real-looking message can still be fake.\n\nHe does not tap the link. He checks with the courier's official app.\n\n💡 Do not tap links or call numbers in such messages. Check yourself, in the official app or at the office.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ What To Do — Step by Step\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Pause\n✅ Do not rush. Fear and hurry are the scammer's tools.\n\n2️⃣ Do Not Tap or Call\n✅ Do not tap the link.\n✅ Do not call the number in the message.\n\n3️⃣ Check Yourself\n📱 Open the official app, or visit the office, and check.\n\n4️⃣ Delete or Report\n✅ Delete the message.\n✅ Tell your family so they are warned too.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mrs. Pandey's Message\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMrs. Pandey gets a message: “Your electricity will be cut tonight. Call this number now.”\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Not call the number\n☐ Not tap any link in the message\n☐ Check in the official electricity app or at the office\n☐ Tell her family about it\n☐ Call the number quickly to avoid the power cut\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Not call the number\n✅ Not tap any link in the message\n✅ Check in the official electricity app or at the office\n✅ Tell her family about it\n❌ Calling the number is the trap\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Fake Spotter Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You can recognise common fake messages\n✅ You do not lose money by tapping a link\n✅ You know where to check: the official app or the office\n✅ You keep your family safe, too\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nHave you ever received a message that rushed you? What did you do?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
