     "title": "Story 4.7 · 🎮 Say No to Strangers",
     "description": "✨ Children: never share your name, school, photos or address with people you meet in games or chats.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Friendly Player\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Rohit\n\n🧒 Rohit is 11 years old and lives in Indore. He loves his online cricket game, and he plays after homework.\n\nOne day, a player he does not know sends him a message in the game chat:\n“Hi, you play so well! What is your name? Which school do you go to? Send me a photo?”\n\nRohit feels special. Nobody has ever praised his playing like this.\nHe is about to type his school's name.\n\nThen he remembers what his teacher said: “Never tell people you meet in games or chats your name, school, photos or address.”\n\n📱 Rohit remembers:\n• A stranger online may not be who they say\n• Never share your name, school, photos or address\n• Tell a parent if someone asks\n\nHe does not answer. He goes straight to his mother and shows her.\n\nHis mother says: *“You did the right thing. I am proud of you.”*\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the Stranger Says “Do Not Tell Your Parents”?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nPriya, 12, gets a message: *“This is our secret. Do not tell your parents.”*\n\nA friendly person never needs a secret from your parents.\nThat is a big warning sign.\n\nShe shows the message to her father at once.\n\n💡 Children: if someone makes you uncomfortable, tell a parent or a teacher. You will never be in trouble for telling.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ For Children and Parents\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Stay Private\n✅ Never tell people you meet in games or chats your name, school, photos or address.\n\n2️⃣ Tell a Parent\n✅ If someone asks for these things, tell a parent.\n\n3️⃣ Friends Only\n✅ Set the game or app chat to friends only.\n\n4️⃣ Talk Often\n✅ Talk to your child about who they meet online.\n✅ Make sure they know they can always tell you anything.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Rohit's Game Chat\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nA stranger in Rohit's game asks for his name, school and a photo.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should Rohit do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Not share his name, school, photo or address\n☐ Tell his mother or father\n☐ Not reply to the stranger\n☐ Send a photo because the player was friendly\n☐ Keep it a secret from his parents\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Not share his name, school, photo or address\n✅ Tell his mother or father\n✅ Not reply to the stranger\n❌ A friendly stranger online can still be unsafe\n❌ Never keep it a secret from your parents\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Stranger Smart Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ Children stay safe in games and chats\n✅ Strangers do not learn where a child lives or studies\n✅ Children know they can always tell a parent\n✅ Parents worry less and talk more\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nParents: when did you last talk to your child about who they chat with online?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
