     "title": "Story 4.8 · 📢 The Golden Hour",
     "description": "✨ Lost money to a fraud? Call 1930 in the first hour, and call your bank.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"The Loan That Was a Trap\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. Saxena\n\n👴 Mr. Saxena is 71 years old and lives in Gwalior. He is a retired clerk.\n\nHe needed a small loan for a family function, and a caller offered one on easy terms.\nHe paid a “processing fee” through UPI. Then another fee. Then another.\n\nSuddenly, he realises: no loan is coming. He has been cheated.\nHis stomach sinks. He feels ashamed and wants to hide it from everyone.\n\nBut then he remembers: “The first hour after a fraud matters most.”\n\n📱 What he does:\n• Calls 1930, the National Cyber Crime Helpline\n• Or reports at cybercrime.gov.in\n• Calls his bank to block his card or UPI\n\nHe calls 1930 and tells them everything.\nThen he calls his bank and asks to block his card and UPI.\n\nActing fast gives the best chance of stopping the loss.\nHis son sits beside him: *“Baba, you did not delay. That is what matters.”*\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If You Feel Too Ashamed to Tell Anyone?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nMrs. Trivedi, 67, loses money to a fake prize call, and she is too embarrassed to tell her family.\nShe waits two days.\n\nEvery hour of waiting makes it harder to act. Cheats are clever, and anyone can be fooled.\n\nWhen she finally tells her daughter, they call 1930 together.\n\n💡 There is no shame in being cheated. Tell someone and act at once.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ What To Do — Step by Step\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Act at Once\n✅ The first hour matters most. Do not wait.\n\n2️⃣ Call 1930\n📱 Call 1930, the National Cyber Crime Helpline.\n✅ Or report at cybercrime.gov.in.\n\n3️⃣ Call Your Bank\n✅ Ask your bank to block your card or UPI.\n\n4️⃣ Tell Your Family\n✅ Tell someone you trust, so they can help you.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Mr. Saxena's Hour\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nMr. Saxena realises that a loan offer was a fraud, and his money has gone through UPI.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should he do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Call 1930 straight away\n☐ Call his bank to block his card or UPI\n☐ Tell a family member\n☐ Wait a few days, hoping it will be fine\n☐ Hide it because he feels ashamed\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Call 1930 straight away\n✅ Call his bank to block his card or UPI\n✅ Tell a family member\n❌ Waiting makes it harder to act\n❌ There is no shame in being cheated, so tell someone\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Quick Responder Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ You know exactly who to call: 1930 and your bank\n✅ You act in the first hour, when it matters most\n✅ You do not hide it out of shame\n✅ You feel prepared, not helpless\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nIs the number 1930 saved in your phone? Who would you tell first if you were cheated?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
