    {
     "title": "Story 6.3 · 📚 The Patient Tutor",
     "description": "✨ Use AI to explain and to test you, not to write your homework.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Fractions at Last\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Divya\n\n🧒 Divya is 12 years old and lives in Mysuru. She finds fractions very confusing.\n\nHer mother cannot help much, and her tuition teacher is busy.\nHer friend says: *“Just ask AI to write the homework. Copy it, and you are done!”*\n\nDivya is tempted. But her teacher always says: *“If you copy, you do not learn.”*\n\nHer mother suggests a better way.\n\n📱 Instead of asking AI to write the homework, she can ask it to:\n• Explain a topic step by step\n• Test her with questions\n\nDivya types: “Explain fractions with a simple example, then give me 3 questions to try.”\n\nThe AI explains with a chocolate bar cut into pieces, then gives her three questions.\nShe tries them. She gets two right and one wrong, and asks the AI to explain the wrong one again.\n\n*“It is like a patient tutor who never gets tired,”* she says.\nAt school the next day, she answers a fractions question in class.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the AI Gives a Wrong Answer?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAman, 13, asks the AI a maths question and gets an answer that does not look right.\n\nAI can make mistakes. He checks it against his textbook and asks his teacher.\n\n💡 Use AI to understand, and always check with your textbook or teacher. Never copy answers without understanding them.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Use AI as a Tutor\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Pick a Topic You Find Hard\n✅ For example, fractions.\n\n2️⃣ Ask for an Explanation\n✅ Ask it to explain step by step, with a simple example.\n\n3️⃣ Ask It to Test You\n✅ Ask for 3 questions to try.\n\n4️⃣ Check and Learn\n✅ Try the questions yourself.\n✅ Ask it to explain again what you got wrong.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Divya's Homework\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nDivya finds fractions hard and wants to use AI the right way.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should she do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Ask AI to explain fractions step by step with a simple example\n☐ Ask AI to give her 3 questions to try\n☐ Try the questions herself\n☐ Ask AI to write the whole homework to copy\n☐ Believe every AI answer without checking\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Ask AI to explain fractions step by step with a simple example\n✅ Ask AI to give her 3 questions to try\n✅ Try the questions herself\n❌ Copying does not help you learn\n❌ AI can make mistakes, so check with your textbook or teacher\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Smart Learner Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes learning this:\n\n✅ Children understand topics instead of copying\n✅ AI becomes a patient tutor, any time\n✅ Children learn to check answers\n✅ Marks and confidence both improve\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhich topic would you like to ask an AI to explain step by step? Parents: how will you talk to your child about using AI honestly?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
