    {
     "title": "Story 6.7 · ⌚ Safe Steps to School",
     "description": "✨ A GPS smartwatch helps you stay connected with your child, used with care and respect.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n📖 Story: \"Aanya Walks to Tuition\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n👤 Meet Mr. and Mrs. Yadav\n\n👨‍👩‍👧 Mr. and Mrs. Yadav live in Noida with their daughter Aanya, who is 9.\n\nEvery evening, Aanya walks to her tuition class, a short way from home.\nHer parents want her to be independent, but they worry.\nA smartphone feels too much for a nine-year-old.\n\nThey choose a GPS smartwatch made for children.\n\n📱 The watch can:\n• Let Aanya call her parents with one tap\n• Let her use an SOS button in an emergency\n• Show her parents where the watch is, in the watch maker's official app\n\nBefore she wears it, they sit down with Aanya and explain what it does, and why.\nShe helps choose her SOS contacts: Mummy, Papa and Dadi.\n\nThat evening, Mrs. Yadav opens the app and sees the watch at the tuition class.\nShe feels calm. Aanya feels trusted.\n\n*“Mummy, it is like you are walking with me,”* says Aanya.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🤔 What If the Watch Cannot Find the Location?\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nOne day, the app shows Aanya at home for an hour, but she is already at tuition.\nThe location is not always exact, and it can be late. The battery may be low, or the signal weak.\n\nMrs. Yadav does not panic. She calls Aanya's watch, then the tuition teacher.\nEverything is fine.\n\n💡 A watch never replaces an adult's care. Keep talking to your child, and teach her to go to a trusted adult if she needs help.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🛠️ How To Use It Safely\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1️⃣ Set It Up With the Official App\n✅ Set up the watch with the watch maker's official app.\n✅ Never install a tracking app sent to you as a link.\n\n2️⃣ Add Only Trusted Contacts\n✅ Add only trusted family members as contacts.\n\n3️⃣ Keep the Location Private\n✅ Never share the watch's location publicly.\n✅ Explain to your child what the watch does, and why.\n\n4️⃣ Charge It Every Night\n✅ Charge the watch every night.\n✅ Remember: it never replaces an adult's care.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🎮 Interactive Activity: \"Aanya's Watch\"\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎬 Scenario\nAanya's parents are setting up her GPS smartwatch.\n\n❓ Question\nWhat should they do? (Tick all that are correct.)\n\n☐ Set it up with the watch maker's official app\n☐ Add only trusted family members as contacts\n☐ Keep the location private\n☐ Charge the watch every night\n☐ Post the watch's map on social media\n\n🔑 Answer\n✅ Set it up with the watch maker's official app\n✅ Add only trusted family members as contacts\n✅ Keep the location private\n✅ Charge the watch every night\n❌ Never share a child's location publicly\n\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n🏆 Safe Steps Guardian Badge Earned!\n🏆━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━🏆\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🌟 Real-Life Benefits\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAfter spending just a few minutes setting it up:\n\n✅ Your child can call you with one tap\n✅ An SOS button is ready for an emergency\n✅ You can see where the watch is\n✅ You and your child feel more at ease\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n💭 Reflection Question\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nHow will you explain to your child why the watch is for care, and not for spying?\n\n🌟 Digital Saathi · Learn it · Try it · Stay safe"
